      "description": "Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (1)The railway between Coleraine and Londonderry is level for nearly all of its 34 miles. There are numerous level crossings both on public roads and on private farm lanes. This is the Barmouth crossing just east of Castlerock where the Barmouth Road runs to the western bank of the River Bann. The view is towards the Ballywoolen Road with the river behind the photographer. Continue to C7835 : Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (2).",
